  "title": "Brahmagupta",
  "summary": "Brahmagupta, born in 598, wrote the 25-chapter Brahmasphutasiddhanta in 628 at Bhillamala, today's Bhinmal, and later headed the astronomical observatory at Ujjain. The book defines zero as the result of subtracting a number from itself and sets rules for arithmetic with negative numbers and zero. He also wrote the Khandakhadyaka in 665.",
